  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of Food Security and Nutrition Observatory for the Mashreq Sub-region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">?	Regular reports: Produce periodic reports on food security in the region, considering all dimensions of food security based on data collected from regional countries, as well as other relevant regional and global data.
?	Analytical information: Provide analytical information and trend reports on the state of food security in regional countries, based on international dynamics related to production prices, transportation, food availability, and food prices.
?	Early warning: Monitor key food security indicators and issue early warning reports and recommendations to regional countries to address potential emergencies.
?	Data collection: Collect data on consumption and local demand to determine the food gap and collect data in the Mashreq countries.
?	Regional plan: Develop a regional plan for the Mashreq to monitor achievements and outputs and identify the regional countries to be included.
?	National food security information system: Develop a national food security information system for monitoring and analysing food security at the global and regional levels.
?	Integration with FAO platform: The observatory will be linked to the FAO&apos;s food security dashboard and the crisis management centre as a starting point for work within Jordan, to be later transferred to neighbouring countries. The observatory can also be linked to the food security information centre being established</narrative>
  </description>
